  "source_binding": "One unchanged snapshot for full workspace checks and fixed release/process acceptance; all crate non-document files, machine contracts, dependencies and toolchain are included.",
  "implementation": [
    "ResourceDomain leases an actual preconfigured cgroup v2 leaf via pinned no-symlink directory FDs and cooperative exclusive inode flock. CPU, NUMA, finite memory.max, swap=0, domain type and empty membership are checked before launch.",
    "A private allocation-free pre_exec hook rechecks settings, migrates the child through a parent-opened cgroup.procs FD, applies exact CPU affinity and verifies the kernel readback before executing the sealed ELF.",
    "Cold observations sample actual group membership, every thread affinity/allowed NUMA nodes and settings, bracketed by supervisor-owned child and immutable executable identity checks.",
    "Supervisor retains the resource domain with the Child entry. Exit does not release the lease or prove all group resources have been reclaimed.",
    "App/Host carry a complete optional three-purpose resource plan through worker, source replay, restore/replay/rebuild rollback probes, and same-PID capture promotion. Any configured resource failure returns an error without unconstrained fallback.",
    "Optional plans omitted from App JSON preserve the existing serialized form and legacy launch behavior. Global projection Applied and OS-account assignment remain separate unfinished work."
  ],
